# Custom Entity Support

I will implement the ability to create simple custom mobs in the Minecraft Mod Maker.

## Proposed Changes

### Data and Infrastructure
#### [MODIFY] [ModElement.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModElement.java)
- Add `boolean isEntity()` to the interface.

#### [NEW] [EntityData.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/EntityData.java)
- Store name, texture, max health, movement speed, attack damage, and spawn egg colors.

### UI Layer
#### [MODIFY] [ModMakerApp.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModMakerApp.java)
- Add a new "Add Entity" tab.
- Fields:
    - Entity Name (TextField)
    - Texture (File Picker)
    - Max Health (JSpinner)
    - Speed (JSpinner)
    - Attack Damage (JSpinner)
    - AI Type (Dropdown: Passive, Neutral, Hostile)
    - Primary Egg Color (TextField/ColorPicker)
    - Secondary Egg Color (TextField/ColorPicker)
- `addEntity` logic and list display update.

### Generation Layer
#### [MODIFY] [ModGenerator.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModGenerator.java)
- Add `DeferredRegister<EntityType<?>> ENTITIES` to the generated main class.
- Update `writeJavaClasses` to:
    - Register entities and spawn eggs.
    - Generate `{EntityName}Entity.java` extending `PathfinderMob`.
    - Generate `{EntityName}Model.java` (using a basic humanoid template).
    - Generate `{EntityName}Renderer.java`.
    - Add an event subscriber for `EntityAttributeCreationEvent`.
    - Add an event subscriber for `EntityRenderersEvent.RegisterRenderers`.
- Update `createAssets` to:
    - Copy entity textures to `assets/{modId}/textures/entity/`.
    - Generate simple spawn egg item models.
    - Add entity and spawn egg entries to `en_us.json`.

## Technical Challenges
> [!WARNING]
> **Client-Side Setup**: Entities require specific client-side only registrations (rendering). I will handle this in the main mod class using `@Mod.EventBusSubscriber` with `value = Dist.CLIENT` to keep the code modular and avoid server-side crashes.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Build and compile check: `mvn clean compile`.

### Manual Verification
1. Launch the app.
2. Navigate to "Add Entity" tab.
3. Configure a "Lava Creeper" with custom red/yellow textures, 100 HP, and high speed.
4. Add it to the queue and generate the mod.
5. Inspect the generated source code for correct entity, model, and renderer classes.
6. Verify that `MainMod.java` includes entity registration and attribute creation.
